{"repositoryId":809814744,"availability":"available","full":"JayCBoal/AutomationApp","name":"AutomationApp","description":"Explore this public GitHub project.","category":"Other","language":"Python","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2024-06-03T13:55:43Z","updated":"2026-10-13T03:45:57Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://jaycboal.github.io/AutomationApp/","topics":[],"demo":"https://jaycboal.github.io/AutomationApp/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-13T07:37:37.354Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-13T07:37:37.354Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-13T07:37:37.354Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-13T07:37:37.354Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["AutoApp is a batch-processing execution framework that keeps what a job does separate from when it runs.","A workload automation scheduler (Control-M, AutoSys, ActiveBatch, RunMyJobs, cron) decides when a job runs and passes AutoApp two things: a job key and its own instance ID. AutoApp looks up the job's steps and parameters in its own database, runs them, and returns an exit code. Because the job definitions live outside the scheduler, changing schedulers does not mean rewriting jobs.","It also keeps a structured record of every file operation, tied to a register of the places files come from and go to, so a file's path through the system can be traced."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/JayCBoal/AutomationApp/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"3f7fad3ad6df0f91f241f91710afa2a4687f05910b7d03f1b544bc7c74abb5bd","extractedAt":"2026-10-13T07:37:37.495Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-13T07:37:37.495Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"AutoApp is a batch-processing execution framework that keeps what a job does separate from when it runs.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/JayCBoal/AutomationApp/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"3f7fad3ad6df0f91f241f91710afa2a4687f05910b7d03f1b544bc7c74ab